---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PromptBlock from '../../components/PromptBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="People cookbook · Pace"
  description="People recipes for the Pace marketplace. Recruiting pipeline status. Interview prep that matches the role. Onboarding day-one without the checklist scramble."
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook/people"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-team-page-head">
      <a class="usecases-back-link" href="/cookbook">&larr; All cookbooks</a>
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">People cookbook</span>
      <h1>People</h1>
      <p class="usecases-team-page-tagline">Recruiting pipeline status. Interview prep that matches the role. Onboarding day-one without the checklist scramble.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="usecases-team-page-body">
<article class="usecase-card usecase-card-marquee">
        <span class="usecase-card-badge">Marquee recipe</span>
        <h3>Weekly recruiting pipeline digest</h3>
        <p class="usecase-outcome">Hiring managers know where every open req stands without asking.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekly Monday 08:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>recruiting-pipeline</code>, <code>people-report</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), ATS connector, Slack delivery</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Hiring managers walk into Monday standup already knowing where every open req stands : candidates aging in a stage, interviews scheduled for the week, offers extended, declines. No more "where are we with X" updates.</p>

        <div class="usecase-setup">
          <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>
          <ol class="usecase-steps">
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Install the human-resources plugin</h5>
                <div class="usecase-step-actions">
                  <a class="usecase-step-btn" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=human-resources" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Install in Cowork &nearr;</a>
                  <code class="usecase-step-cmd">claude plugin install human-resources@pace</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Authorize your ATS + Slack</h5>
                <p>Most ATSes (Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever, and others) don't have first-party MCP servers yet. The skill still works against pasted exports, structured docs in Notion, or via the Custom URL pattern in the <a href="/docs/connectors">connector docs</a>. If you want us to set this up against your specific ATS, <a href="mailto:hello@goldenberry.so">talk to GoldenBerry</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Create the scheduled routine</h5>
                <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>Schedule</strong> &middot; <strong>Weekly</strong> &middot; <strong>Monday</strong> &middot; <strong>08:00</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">4</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>
                <PromptBlock prompt={`Run recruiting-pipeline against the
ATS. For each open requisition, surface:

  - Stage of every active candidate
  - Time-in-stage (flag anyone > 10 business days)
  - Interviews scheduled this week (panel + candidate names)
  - Offers extended / accepted / declined since last week
  - Reqs without any candidates in pipeline ("stuck")

Format as a digest grouped by hiring manager. Post to
#hiring-weekly in Slack. Tag each hiring manager next
to their reqs so they get a heads-up DM.`} />
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">5</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>
                <p>Eyeball the first digest for accuracy (does aging match what you see in the ATS?). Once you trust it, Mondays at 08:00 are automatic.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Interview prep tailored to the role and the candidate</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, API trigger fired by your calendar webhook (filter on "interview")</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>interview-prep</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (API trigger), ATS + Apollo connectors, plan mode</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>When an interview lands on the calendar, <code>interview-prep</code> pulls the JD, candidate resume, and prior round feedback. It drops a prep brief into the event description: focus areas, suggested probing questions, and what to avoid re-asking. Panel walks in calibrated.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>1:1 prep brief, in the manager's inbox 30 minutes before the meeting</h3>
        <p>Before every 1:1, a routine assembles a brief: what the direct has shipped (Linear, GitHub), what they've blocked on (Slack threads, open PRs), what came up in the last 1:1 notes. Manager walks into the meeting with the picture instead of asking "so what have you been up to?".</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, calendar webhook 30 min before any 1:1 event</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>onboarding-plan</code>, <code>review-feedback</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (calendar webhook), Linear + GitHub + Slack + Notion connectors</dd></div>
        </dl>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the API-triggered routine</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>API</strong>. Save and copy the routine URL + bearer token; point the upstream webhook at it (e.g. calendar provider, Intercom webhook, PagerDuty webhook, depending on the trigger).</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`30 minutes before any 1:1 on my calendar, assemble a brief on the direct I'm meeting with:

- What they shipped this week (Linear closed, GitHub merged).
- What they're stuck on (open PRs over 3 days old, Slack threads where they pinged me, blocked Linear tickets).
- What came up in our last 1:1 notes in Notion.

Drop the brief into the calendar event description so I see it when I open the meeting.`} label="1:1 prep prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>
      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Offer letter drafted from the candidate record</h3>
        <p>Hiring manager clicks "send offer" in the ATS. A routine pulls the candidate's role, level, band, and recruiter notes, then drafts the offer letter from your standard template with the right compensation, equity grant, and start-date language. People ops reviews and sends. 40 minutes per offer becomes 5.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, API trigger fired by ATS stage-change to "offer"</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>job-description</code>, <code>comp-analysis</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (API trigger), ATS data (via Notion exports or Custom URL), plan mode for people-ops review</dd></div>
        </dl>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the API-triggered routine</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>API</strong>. Save and copy the routine URL + bearer token; point the upstream webhook at it (e.g. calendar provider, Intercom webhook, PagerDuty webhook, depending on the trigger).</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`When a candidate hits the "offer" stage in our ATS, pull their record: role, level, band, recruiter notes, start date. Draft the offer letter from our standard template with the right comp (base + variable), equity grant per the band, and start-date language.

Park the draft in plan mode for people-ops to review. Once approved, the recruiter sends from the ATS.`} label="Offer letter prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="usecases-footer">
      <p>
        Have a people workflow that should live here? <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues/new">Open an issue</a> with the trigger, skills, and Claude features it uses; we'll fold it into the cookbook.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .usecases-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .usecases-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .usecases-lede strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Engineering callout above the TOC */
  .usecases-eng-callout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out-quart);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecases-eng-callout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  /* TOC grid */
  .usecases-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .usecases-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin: 0 6px var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .usecases-toc-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-toc-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .usecases-toc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .usecases-team {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .usecases-team-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-team-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-team-tagline {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecase-card-marquee {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 92%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .usecase-card-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecase-card-badge::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .usecase-card > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }
  /* Meta: small chip row at the bottom (was a big dl block at top) */
  .usecase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta > div {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .usecase-meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .usecase-meta dt::after {
    content: ":";
    margin-left: 1px;
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .usecase-meta dd code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .usecase-card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-footer {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-footer a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch a,
  .usecases-impeccable-when a,
  .usecases-team-tagline a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch code,
  .usecases-impeccable-when code,
  .usecases-team-tagline code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::before {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-right: var(--spacing-sm);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when p,
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecase-meta > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }

